plicit child-test requirement) verifying Jira Cloud write scope drops DIG while preserving remaining required write scopes.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Jira Cloud write scope loses DIG'","AC5 covers bridge factories preserving auth lifecycles but does not name the DIG scope change","'Other auth, redaction, retry, TLS, and output behavior changes require an explicit child decision and test.'"],"finding":"The Explicit corrections state 'Jira Cloud write scope loses DIG' as a concrete behavior delta, but no acceptance criterion covers verifying this scope removal (both that DIG is removed and that remaining scopes still function).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7289a6a1f68d494e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Explicit corrections; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n18d413dbf0984908","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A child implements bridge composition but silently retains DIG, or removes it without a test proving remaining write scope still works."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend AC5 or add an AC: 'Jira Cloud write composition no longer requests DIG scope, and bridge write operations succeed under the reduced scope set, verified by an offline oracle and bounded live canary.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Jira Cloud write scope loses `DIG`'","'tracker layout reaches every owner'","No AC line names DIG scope or tracker-layout propagation as a verified outcome"],"finding":"The 'Explicit corrections' list names concrete behavior changes — 'Jira Cloud write scope loses DIG' and 'tracker layout reaches every owner' — that do not map to any acceptance criterion; the ACs cover precedence/root and consumer projections generally but no criterion verifies these specific deltas.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdca1870fc8a27a55","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope > Explicit corrections; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n08a0fdcfd639eea1","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the child that cuts the ordinary CLI ticket/store command path and the public Python library operations from shadow to authoritative OperationSnapshot/runtime-binding consumption (or extend S1/S7 scope), so parent AC1/AC2 are covered authoritatively rather than only in shadow.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3","G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["S1 Compatibility/rollback: 'Shadow composition does not control execution.'","S1 Plan 3: 'Existing execution remains authoritative; shadow comparison emits only version, source kinds, and a redacted fingerprint.'","S2 Outcome scopes only 'reconcile-check and dry-run fetch/diff/preflight paths'; S3 Outcome scopes only 'write/apply and subprocess paths.'","S5 scopes only MCP and review-bot startup bindings.","Parent Scope: 'all affected CLI/library/MCP/reconciler/hosted consumers'; parent AC2 requires every affected consumer to receive an immutable binding with no in-progress reread.","Roster cross-check: no sibling's indented ACs deliver an authoritative (non-shadow) cutover of the ordinary CLI ticket/store command or the public Python library ticket-store operations.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"No sibling cuts the non-reconciler CLI ordinary ticket/store command path (and the public Python library operations) from shadow-only snapshot composition to AUTHORITATIVE runtime-binding consumption. S1 explicitly keeps execution on the legacy path ('Shadow composition does not control execution'; 'Existing execution remains authoritative'). S2 and S3 cut only the reconciler read/check and apply paths; S5 cuts MCP and review-bot; S4 cuts LLM; S6 cuts op-cert. The parent's Scope names 'all affected CLI/library/MCP/reconciler/hosted consumers' and AC2 requires 'Every affected consumer receives an immutable projection/runtime binding and no in-progress operation rereads ambient state,' and AC1 requires CLI/Python to 'produce equivalent non-secret behavior from the approved precedence/root contract' — an authoritative, not shadow, guarantee.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc1511a05c96ddca1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11 (S1); owned-by-none gap across the roster","norm_id":"n941d5052d7141dc0","priority":0.8125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A `rebar` CLI ordinary ticket create/update command (not reconcile) still resolves config through the legacy ambient path after RP-04 completes, so an in-progress operation could reread environment/cwd — violating parent AC2.","A public Python library ticket-store operation runs on legacy composition; S7 removes legacy facades but no child made this consumer authoritative on the snapshot first, risking either an uncovered consumer or a broken removal."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add (or extend an existing child's scope for) an authoritative cutover of the non-reconciler CLI ticket/store commands and public Python library operations to consume the immutable OperationSnapshot binding with a no-in-progress-reread oracle, and pin its removal-precondition proof in S7.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC5: 'Git and bridge factories preserve provider-native auth lifecycles and instantiate only the selected integration; missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback.'","S3 (6e3b) ACs name only DIG/Cloud-write-scope fail-closed and child-env; the Git push auth-lifecycle / fail-before-network outcome appears only in S3 Testing ('Failure-injection tests cover missing project/auth, revoked credential'), not as an AC.","S2 (e042) AC4 covers this outcome for Jira only; S5 (5851) AC3 covers it for review-bot Gerrit/GitHub only — neither exceeds scope to the reconciler/store Git push factory.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"Parent AC5's Git half is only partially covered: no child's acceptance criteria assert that the Git factory 'preserves provider-native auth lifecycles', 'instantiates only the selected integration', and that 'missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback' for Git specifically. S2 (e042) delivers this for the Jira bridge only, and S5 (5851) for review-bot Gerrit/GitHub only. S3 (6e3b) is the child that threads GitRuntime and owns Git adapter/ref/lock/push, but its enumerated ACs cover only (a) apply/Git/delivery paths completing with poisoned resolvers, (b) the Cloud-write/DIG fail-closed case, (c) child-env, (d) no-global-mutation, (e) provider-neutral regression, (f) facade rollback — none states the Git auth-lifecycle-preservation or the fail-before-Git-push-without-alternate-principal outcome as an acceptance criterion. S3 mentions 'revoked credential' only inside a Testing bullet, not as an AC oracle.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f75bfee7f9fe88d68","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6 (RP-04 S3); cross-checked against child e042 (S2) and child 5851 (S5)","norm_id":"n421d9d6195b28a91","priority":0.8125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Promote S3's Git failure-injection scenario to an explicit S3 acceptance criterion mirroring S2 AC4 but scoped to GitRuntime/push (fail before network/write, no alternate-principal fallback, only selected integration, lifecycle preserved).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries'","'reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live canaries'","No definition of 'bounded' (count/cost/time)"],"finding":"Multiple ACs and design bullets require 'bounded live' canaries (e.g. 'bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries', 'bounded-live canaries') without stating the bound (request count, cost, or time), leaving the executor to guess the limit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f96396b4cf7aeb438","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (LLM cutover bullet; operator-attested bullet)","norm_id":"n5105038bbef98521","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a default such as 'bounded = at most N live requests per provider per canary run' to the plan.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/config.md: a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11 & aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4 (no ordering edge)","docs/env-vars.md: 6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6 & 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 (no ordering edge)","docs/reuse-surface.md: 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 & bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06 (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_store/push.py: 6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6 & 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 (no ordering edge)","tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py: 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 & bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06 (no ordering edge)"],"finding":"Sibling tickets touch the same file(s) with no ordering edge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82524518cbf636a6","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"na0177dc3af65d74f","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a depends_on/blocks edge to serialize, or partition the file ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["9 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[operator-attested] AWS review-bot and reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live can' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Assign an authoritative owner for the 'CLI input outranks environment for tracker.dir' correction on any non-reconciler CLI ticket-store command, or state that tracker.dir is consumed exclusively by reconciler paths already covered by S2/S3.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7094,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent Explicit corrections: 'CLI input outranks environment for tracker.dir.'","S1 proves 'Explicit input wins each pairwise precedence case' but only in shadow (execution remains legacy).","S2 AC: 'Supplied config and custom tracker directory/branch/remote determine every observed read/ref/query owner' — scoped to reconciler read/check; S3 to apply/Git. Roster shows no sibling enforcing CLI-over-env tracker.dir precedence authoritatively for non-reconciler CLI ticket-store commands.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"The parent's explicit correction 'CLI input outranks environment for tracker.dir' has no authoritative owner for the non-reconciler CLI path. S1 proves the precedence pair in shadow only; S2/S3 apply custom tracker directory/branch/remote solely within reconciler read and apply paths. If any non-reconciler CLI command consumes tracker.dir, no sibling's ACs authoritatively enforce CLI-over-environment precedence for it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffa7a5b9005a3f04d","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"child a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11 (S1); cross-roster absence for non-reconciler tracker.dir consumers","norm_id":"n6368da00db8d3481","priority":0.2406,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A CLI ticket-store command with an explicit tracker.dir flag but a conflicting REBAR tracker env var could still honor the environment on the authoritative path, since only shadow (S1) proved the precedence and the authoritative reconciler-only cutovers (S2/S3) do not cover this command."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Confirm and document that tracker.dir is consumed only by reconciler paths (covered by S2/S3); otherwise extend the cutover story from the prior finding to include an authoritative CLI-over-environment tracker.dir precedence oracle.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"insufficient","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","in